Call `Nodrix.begin()` in `setup()` with your Wi-Fi and cloud credentials, then call `Nodrix.run()` on every pass of `loop()` so the socket is serviced.

```cpp
void setup() {
  Nodrix.begin(WIFI_SSID, WIFI_PASS, HOST, TOKEN);
}

void loop() {
  Nodrix.run();
}
```

Use the `NODRIX_WRITE` macro at file scope. It runs whenever the cloud writes that variable, and the library acks the write for you.

```cpp
NODRIX_WRITE("led") {
  digitalWrite(LED_BUILTIN, value.asBool());
}
```

Delivery is at-least-once, so keep the handler idempotent.

`value` is a `NodrixValue`. Convert it with `asBool()`, `asInt()`, `asLong()`, `asFloat()`, `asDouble()` or `asString()`, and guard with `isNull()` when a variable may not be set yet.

```cpp
NODRIX_WRITE("brightness") {
  if (value.isNull()) return;
  analogWrite(PIN, value.asInt());
}
```

Register each network with `Nodrix.addAP()` before `begin()`, then call the two-argument `begin()` that takes only host and token. The strongest reachable network wins, with automatic failover.

```cpp
Nodrix.addAP("home", "pass1");
Nodrix.addAP("workshop", "pass2");
Nodrix.begin(HOST, TOKEN);
```

`send()` is overloaded for `bool`, `int`, `long`, `float`, `double`, `const char*` and `String`. The first argument is always the variable name your widget is bound to.

```cpp
Nodrix.send("temperature", 23.5f);
Nodrix.send("uptime_s", (long)(millis() / 1000));
Nodrix.send("status", "ok");
```

Register callbacks with `Nodrix.onConnect()` and `Nodrix.onDisconnect()` before `begin()`, and read `Nodrix.connected()` for the current state.

```cpp
Nodrix.onConnect([]() { Serial.println("up"); });
Nodrix.onDisconnect([]() { Serial.println("down"); });
```

Call `Nodrix.setCACert()` with a PEM string before `begin()`. Certificate pinning survives server certificate rotation as long as the root is unchanged, so prefer it to a fingerprint.

```cpp
Nodrix.setCACert(NODRIX_ROOT_CA);
Nodrix.begin(WIFI_SSID, WIFI_PASS, HOST, TOKEN);
```

Use HTTP mode: `beginHTTP()`, one `poll()` per wake to push readings and pick up any queued control writes, then sleep.

```cpp
void setup() {
  Nodrix.beginHTTP(WIFI_SSID, WIFI_PASS, HOST, TOKEN);
  Nodrix.send("temperature", readTemp());
  Nodrix.poll();
  esp_deep_sleep_start();
}
```

One `NODRIX_WRITE` handler per bound variable.

```cpp
NODRIX_WRITE("light_living") {
  digitalWrite(RELAY_A, value.asBool());
}

NODRIX_WRITE("light_bedroom") {
  digitalWrite(RELAY_B, value.asBool());
}
```

As often as you have a genuinely new reading, but throttle the loop with a `millis()` gate rather than sending every pass — an unthrottled `loop()` will send thousands of times a second.

```cpp
if (millis() - lastSend > 5000) {
  lastSend = millis();
  Nodrix.send("temperature", t);
}
```
